aarch64 #11: cache vchroot_run's per-component lstat to kill redundant path-translation stats.

vchroot_run lstat()s every accumulated path component on every guest path translation, so a dyld load
re-walks the same read-only system directories thousands of times: measured 94% of newfstatat redundant
(3379 total, 184 unique; /usr/lib/system re-stat'd ~400x per spawn) under `cider shell`. Add a per-process
cache of the dominant "this accumulated path exists and is not a symlink" result, keyed by the full path
and tagged with a generation counter that the namespace-mutating syscall wrappers (unlink/rename/symlink)
bump, so a cached entry can never outlive the path being removed or retyped. Symlinks and ENOENT bypass the
cache and keep full semantics. Disabled under TEST (the standalone vchroot test harness).
---
--- a/darling/src/libsystem_kernel/emulation/include/linux_premigration/vchroot_expand.h
+++ b/darling/src/libsystem_kernel/emulation/include/linux_premigration/vchroot_expand.h
@@ -26,4 +26,8 @@
 int vchroot_unexpand(struct vchroot_unexpand_args* args);
 int vchroot_fdpath(struct vchroot_fdpath_args* args);
 
+// aarch64 perf (#11): bumped by namespace-mutating syscalls to invalidate the
+// vchroot_run stat cache (vchroot_userspace.c).
+void __vchroot_bump_generation(void);
+
 #endif // _VCHROOT_EXPAND_H
--- a/darling/src/libsystem_kernel/emulation/src/linux_premigration/vchroot_userspace.c
+++ b/darling/src/libsystem_kernel/emulation/src/linux_premigration/vchroot_userspace.c
